
  PARTITION FUNCTIONS EVERYWHERE: H(T), THE n+2 RECURSION, AND THE GAME SPECTRUM
======================================================================

  (1) [PROVED] Z_n = sum_T H(T) = n! * 2^(C(n,2)-(n-1))
      n=2: Z_n=2 = 2  (True)
      n=3: Z_n=12 = 12  (True)
      n=4: Z_n=192 = 192  (True)
      n=5: Z_n=7680 = 7680  (True)

  (2) [VERIFIED] n->n+2 recursion: source+sink (transitive boundary) preserves H
      H_(n+2)(inner, transitive boundary) == H_n(inner) over 3000 trials: True
      => the 'add a layer' gadget; nesting it = the infinite-Go recursive value build.

  (3,4) [PROVED/VERIFIED] H multiplicative over strong components =>
      achievable H = monoid <strong H-values>; gaps {7,21} = non-strong-non-product.
      strong H-values (n<=6): [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19, 23, 25, 27, 29, 31, 33, 37, 41, 43, 45]
      7 strong? False; 21 strong? False  (both NO)
      monoid <strong> odd gaps <=45: [7, 21, 35]

  (5) [ANALOGY] H mult/strong-comp <-> game value additive/disjunctive-sum (infinite Go);
      strong H = indecomposable gadget values; H-gaps {7,21} <-> unreachable game values.
  (6) [HONEST] 0.014: UD excess (lower bound) ~ Cl_2(pi/3)-1=0.01494 (prime-3, proved
      structural) ~ root ratios; equality UNVERIFIED. Shape param s=a1/sqrt(a2) real,
      SC-maximized (ULC); 'growth = 0.014' conjectural.

======================================================================
  SUMMARY: H(T) is a partition function (Z_n=n!2^...), multiplicative over strong
  components (disjunctive game sum / cluster expansion), with an n->n+2
  value-building recursion (the infinite-Go gadget). Achievable H = monoid of
  strong H-values; the gaps {7,21} are exactly the non-strong non-products. The
  H-value spectrum is the tournament analogue of the infinite-Go ordinal
  game-value spectrum. Partition functions everywhere: H, the LRC depth
  polynomial, the independence polynomial, and game values are one species.

